# Normalise line endings on the way into git.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout committed CRLF into the tree while the Gen8
# deployment reads and rewrites the same files with LF. `git diff` on the live box
# then reported 2,079 changed lines across five backend modules when the real
# change was 186 insertions and 18 deletions -- the signal was buried under a 10x
# noise floor, and "is production carrying uncommitted fixes?" became unanswerable
# at a glance.
#
# text=auto: store text as LF in the repo, check out native on Windows.
* text=auto

# Always LF: these run on Linux (the Gen8) and CRLF breaks shebangs and heredocs.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# Never touched -- normalising these corrupts them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.gguf  binary
